### What this track proposes
The track adds two sections to the www Tutor Advantage page in en, th, and zh. Phase 1 builds a pure satang-exact commission module, a client calculator with three example presets, a one-level leg payout graph, and a decorative rate curve. Phase 2 adds a gallery of three blurred screenshots from the delivered set and replaces the two "We do not publish income figures" live lines with copy that points at the calculator examples. The zh block takes the English lines until the contracted Chinese speaker delivers. No push happens before the PM page-check, and no deploy command runs. The spec states this intent itself in sections 1, 2, and D-13.

### How the current system works, per this spec
The page is a server component that reads copy with getScopedI18n from a locale file with en, th, and zh blocks. Its sections are hero, process, tutorRole, commitments, and faq; tutorRole.points[3] and faq.items[5].answer still say no income figures are published. A productPictures manifest and the ProductPicture and SectionHeader components already exist for other pages. The commission truth lives in the finance-mlm-service formula; this track re-implements it as a display-only pure module in the www app, with the rate curve and the 3% withholding tax.

### Findings
- F1 [Blocker] plan.md task 2.1: the test that asserts the three manifest keys, their widths and heights, and the file existence has no named file; task 2.1's Done line says "one test asserts the three manifest keys" without a path, and no existing manifest test exists to extend (the only test importing productPictures is src/__tests__/products-page-pictures.red.test.tsx, which belongs to the products overview page, track A-62). Rationale: the plan leaves a file-location choice to the implementer. Smallest fix: name the test file in task 2.1 (for example the Phase 2 locale test or a named new file).
- F2 [Major] spec.md 6.3 items[1] and Thai table: the lessonPhases alt "Tutor app showing the 18 phases of one lesson" (en, line 553) and the Thai alt "แอปติวเตอร์แสดง 18 ช่วงของบทเรียนหนึ่งบท" (line 569) name the tutor app, but the mapped source student-mobile/002-screen.png is a student-app screen (student bottom tab bar, student points header), and spec 6.1 classifies student-mobile/ as the student app; the spec marks only presets[2] and chart as drafts, so the wrong alt is built unmarked, and the note at lines 574-575 verifies only the "18 phases" part. Rationale: published alt text will mislabel the picture it describes; needs a spec change before Phase 2 Red. Smallest fix: mark the slot-2 alt as a draft for PR like D-2a, or correct it to a student-app wording and record the deviation from copy v0.1.
- F3 [Major] spec.md D-9 line 234, D-11 line 253, 6.3 line 544: the citations "(design rule 3)", "(design rule 7)", "(design rule 8)" point at a numbered design-rules list that exists in no readable file (measure/, docs/, and measure/archive/ all searched); the substance of each rule is stated inline, so the numbers dangle. Rationale: an undefined project-specific term. Smallest fix: drop the numbered citations or name the document that holds the list.
- F4 [Nit] spec.md AC-3 / plan.md task 1.1 item 4: the conservation check read as exact equality on baht Numbers fails for preset 2 in JS float (8010 + 4645.69 !== 12655.69); the assertion must compare satang integers or use toBeCloseTo. Smallest fix: one clause in plan task 1.1 ("compare in satang integers").
- F5 [Nit] spec.md D-2 line 143: "Every money figure in the brief matches this table" is false at satang level for preset 2: the brief's table (handoff line 145) gives gross 12,655.70 and net 4,506.33, while D-2 gives 12,655.69 and 4,506.32; the claim holds only at whole-baht rounding (lines 136-137). Smallest fix: qualify the sentence with "to the whole baht".
- F6 [Nit] spec.md 6.3 line 575: the note quotes student-mobile/002 as showing "ขั้นที่ 2/18"; the delivered screen shows "ขั้นที่ 8/18". Smallest fix: correct the quoted phase number.

### Check results (one result per requested check)

1. Paraphrase — PASS. The spec states its intent itself (sections 1, 2, D-4, D-13); no comprehension gap. Both paraphrase sections above are the reviewer's own words.
2. Order fit — PASS. The spec does the ordered work only: new screenshots (6.1-6.3), a commission calculator with networking examples (three presets with legs, D-2), and Daniel's shape (personal students, legs with students by leg, a payout graph, D-4/D-9). The two live-line changes come from PR copy v0.1 section 5, not from this spec. The rate curve is allowed by the PM handoff spec section 5; the second level and a URL parameter are out of scope (section 7).
3. Money math — D-2 AND D-3 ARE RIGHT; the orchestrator's figures are not. Exact numbers (node, D-3 algorithm: rateUnits = round(rate*1e9), gvSatang, BigInt division truncating):
   - Six check values to four decimals: 1,000 → 40.5000%; 5,000 → 42.5000%; 10,000 → 45.0000%; 20,000 → 50.0000%; 30,000 → 55.606455% → 55.6065%; 50,000 → 60.631497% → 60.6315%. Asymptote 0.5/0.7 = 71.4286%. Rate at 1e9 = 71.422028% < 71.43%.
   - Preset 1: GV 12,000, rate 46%, gross 5,520.00, leg payouts 0, tax 165.60, net 5,354.40.
   - Preset 2: rate(24000) = 52.732082% → 52.7321%; flatSatang = 1,265,569 → gross 12,655.69 (raw float rate*24000 = 12,655.699605442065 — the orchestrator's 12,655.70 comes from rounding, but D-3 truncates, and the payout graphic states truncation with rate scale 10^9 as the code truth); leg payouts 4,005.00 each = 8,010.00; payout 4,645.69; tax floor(464,569×3/100) = 139.37; net 4,506.32. Same result with rateUnits truncated instead of rounded.
   - Preset 3: rate(33000) = 56.695275% → 56.6953%; flatSatang 1,870,944 → gross 18,709.44; leg payouts 4,005.00 each = 12,015.00; payout 669,444 satang = 6,694.44; tax 20,083 satang = 200.83; net 649,361 satang = 6,493.61.
   - Conservation holds in satang integers: preset 2: 801,000 + 464,569 = 1,265,569; preset 3: 1,201,500 + 669,444 = 1,870,944. It holds by construction (payout_sat = gross_sat − Σ leg_sat). Note F4: exact equality on baht Numbers fails in float for preset 2.
   - D-1's quotes match the graphic and recompute exactly (62.008093% × 60,000 → 37,204.85; 14,663.41; 10,661.28; 11,880.16).
4. Consistency — the findings above (F1 plan gap, F5, F6, F4). No duplicated or contradictory figures between D-2, D-2a, 5.4, and the plan; preset 2 and 3 strings agree everywhere; the dict insertion order (tutorRole, screens, calculator, faq) is consistent between 5.4 and plan 2.2; every task maps to an AC and every AC to a task (except the F1 file gap); all gates name existing scripts and baselines.
5. Repo truth — PASS. Every named path, component, and symbol exists: product-pictures.ts (shape {src,width,height,portrait}), product-picture.tsx (props {picture, alt}), section-header.tsx (eyebrow/title/description), globals.css, page.tsx and page.test.tsx, getScopedI18n, TutorClassStepper, the locale file with en/th/zh at lines 1/277/553 and the two old live lines at 151 and 182, package name www-reading-advantage, scripts test/build/lint/check-types, turbo check-types, ratchet baseline lintWarnings 241 and copies 36, affected-apps.mjs with --base/--head, heavy-run.sh. The page renders tutorRole, commitments, faq in the order section 2 assumes.
6. Copy truth and gates — PASS with F2. Sixteen en strings and seven th strings match the PR copy file word for word (scripted check); the only intended deviation is the D-2a preset-3 draft, which correctly replaces the superseded two-level preset 3. No forbidden D-16 claim in the new strings; "example" wording present (description, disclaimer); the only percentages are rate values and the 3% tax that the code-truth section carries. Both old live lines exist at the stated keys and disappear in Phase 2.
7. Screens — PASS with F2 and F6 noted. The three sources exist at the stated sizes (070 and 002 at 520x1125, 062 at 1440x900), none is on the README do-not-use list, and the plan's four 062 blur locations match the screen. Slot 1 (070) shows the next class, the lesson, and a chat button, no Reedy card — the mismatch is tracked as open question 3. Slot 2's caption fits (the screen shows ขั้นที่ 8/18), but its alt names the tutor app — untracked, F2.
8. Zero decision — PASS except F1. Leg add/remove (5.2 rule 6: keep first entries, append 3, drop the rest), first paint (D-6: price 3,000, 0 own, 0 legs, zero line, 0 values), preset resets the price (D-5), edit clears the preset (D-7), zh block (D-10: English values, one comment, existing zh translations unchanged), input clamping, tax on zero, display formats, explain variant, rate curve, bar-width mechanism, and component boundary are all answered.
9. Testability — PASS with F1. AC-1..AC-4 → tutor-commission.test.ts; AC-5/7/8 → the locale test; AC-6 → the same locale test; AC-9 → the component test; AC-10 → page.test.tsx; AC-11/12 → gate commands and git diff; AC-13 → the page test plus the unnamed manifest test (F1); AC-14 and AC-15 are written as reviews with named owners (D-14, task 2.5 [b] PM gate), not as tests; AC-16 → the selector command.

Verdict: CHANGES_REQUIRED. One blocker (F1), two majors (F2, F3), three nits (F4, F5, F6). The blockers and majors need a spec or plan change before the touched phase's Red; F2 and F3 can be fixed in one small spec edit alongside F1's plan edit.

